WEBVTT

00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:13,770
Do you recommend repeating a Dutch test periodically?

00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:17,490
Absolutely, because, well, your cortisol level is going

00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:21,410
to change, and I will say this, if you're going to do a cortisol

00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:25,490
test, either through the Dutch test or the adrenal stress profile,

00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:31,370
you really have to do it on a day that's a normal day.

00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:36,490
Because if your normal is fairly in your mind, fairly

00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:42,250
stress-free, but then you had a super stressful day.

00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,930
And it's going to show.

00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:47,570
And then on that day, you do the adrenal stress profiles.

00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:49,370
It's not going to be a real test.

00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:53,770
So you want to do what you would consider your normal day.

00:00:53,770 --> 00:00:55,370
It might be very stressful.

00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:57,890
But if that's, if you're under a lot of stress all the time,

00:00:57,890 --> 00:01:05,210
you want to know what your cortisol levels are on an average time.

00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:11,690
So if it was just a day full of stress,

00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:15,770
and you run it, then you lose the value of it.

00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:18,050
So you lose them out because your cortisol levels

00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:24,090
are going to go up and down, depending on your stress levels.

00:01:24,090 --> 00:01:28,330
Your cortisol is released by your adrenal glands

00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:30,610
and functions on many different levels.

00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:33,650
And at one of the levels, it's a breakdown

00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:34,850
like it in stores.

